8. DATE, TIMEZONE, AND LIFECYCLE RELIABILITY

Do not depend on a single exact-midnight timer to update the application.

Android may suspend the application, kill its process, delay background work, or leave it closed across multiple days.

Implement a reliable date-transition mechanism using the existing architecture.

Required lifecycle behavior

Check or refresh date-dependent state when appropriate:

- The application enters the foreground.
- The application is recreated after process death.
- Relevant dashboard or date-sensitive screens become active.
- Existing background scheduling mechanisms run.
- A local date boundary is detected.

Use the existing lifecycle and scheduling mechanisms where practical.

Do not add unnecessary services, dependencies, alarms, or background workers.

The application must recover correctly even if it misses the actual midnight moment.

Idempotency

The same new-day transition may be detected multiple times.

Ensure that repeated checks:

- Do not create duplicate tasks.
- Do not duplicate Focus sessions.
- Do not increment streaks repeatedly.
- Do not reset historical data.
- Do not create duplicate daily snapshots.
- Do not send duplicate notifications solely because the date check ran again.

Prefer deterministic derivation from existing records over destructive one-time reset operations.

If a stored transition marker is needed, use the smallest safe mechanism consistent with the existing architecture.

Timezone and clock changes

- Preserve historical timestamps.
- Use the project's established timezone convention consistently.
- Calculate local-day boundaries correctly.
- Do not assume every calendar day contains exactly 24 hours.
- Do not delete records when the device timezone changes.
- Do not silently rewrite historical timestamps.
- Recompute date-dependent display values when necessary.
- Handle a device clock moving forward or backward without duplicate session or task creation.

If the app supports multiple time zones or server timestamps, distinguish absolute timestamps from local display dates.

Document any existing limitation instead of claiming unsupported timezone behavior.

